ext and very important is beyond prod  the cloud native security approach  with strong security defaults gke offers  cluster security beyond platform  hardening and os patching  the clusters in gke natively support  kubernetes network policy to restrict  traffic with pod level firewall rules  you can verify  and force and improve the security of  infrastructure components and packages  used for your container images  with the sandbox feature you get a  second layer of defense between  containerized workloads on gke  for enhanced workload security you also  get  built-in support for a wide range of  compliance standards  in short you get beyond fraud security  google's cloud native security approach  for your workloads  and we are on number five much needed to  navigate change  the only constant in our lives scale  whether you want to simplify your  infrastructure management  have batch processing needs or simply  looking to run  internet scale apps and absorb large  spikes in traffic  with gke you are in luck because  starting with 1.18  gke provides the most supported nodes of  any cloud-based kubernetes service and  three times the number of nodes  supported by open source kubernetes  how's that for five and five  are you ready to get started to  celebrate gke's fifth birthday we've got  something special for you  check out this link to learn more  [Music]

